# Build-context hygiene for `context: ./frontend` (docker-compose.yml:124-126).  There was NO
# .dockerignore anywhere in this repo, so the builder stage's `COPY . .` (frontend/Dockerfile:9) —
# which runs AFTER the deps stage's `npm ci` — copied the HOST's node_modules over the container's
# Linux install (measured on this host: the only @next/swc binary present is
# @next/swc-win32-x64-msvc, i.e. the classic "Failed to load SWC binary" build) and the host's .next
# over the build cache, plus hundreds of MB of build context.

node_modules/
.next/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# NOT excluded on purpose: `public/` and `.next/static` — the runner stage copies both explicitly
# (frontend/Dockerfile:19-21).  Everything else here is regenerated inside the image.
#
# `.env*` are not needed: NEXT_PUBLIC_* arrive as build ARGs/ENV (frontend/Dockerfile:12-13), and a
# copied env file would only make the build depend on the host.
.env
.env.*

# Host-side test/coverage output is not part of the image.
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
